00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:55.040
income rather than rapid appreciation of ownership stakes in private companies. When a single

00:03:55.040 --> 00:04:01.660
firm's valuation jumps through an IPO, the resulting paper wealth often escapes immediate taxation

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:08.360
until shares are sold, creating a timing gap that older rules never anticipated. This structure

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:14.160
rewards long-term holding of growth assets while limiting annual revenue from unrealized gains,

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:20.680
a mechanism that has persisted across multiple decades of market evolution. Next time you see a

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:27.140
